 ## Overview
-Occupancy Grid Update is a method to periodically refresh a 3D occupancy grid by querying a Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) model for density at grid voxel centers and marking voxels as occupied if the density exceeds a specified threshold [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of accelerating ray marching by skipping empty space during training and rendering [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its siblings, such as [Occupancy Map Generation via Ray Casting](8136-occupancy-map-generation-via-ray-casting.md), by directly evaluating the neural network's output on a regular lattice rather than casting rays through the scene to infer occupancy [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+Occupancy Grid Update is a method to periodically refresh a 3D occupancy grid by querying a Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) model for density at grid voxel centers and marking voxels as occupied if the density exceeds a specified threshold [S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of accelerating ray marching by skipping empty space during training and rendering [S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its sibling, [Occupancy Map Generation via Ray Casting](8136-occupancy-map-generation-via-ray-casting.md), by directly evaluating the neural network's output on a regular lattice rather than casting rays through the scene to infer occupancy [S2, unofficial].
 
