 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Precision:** Floating-point comparisons at the threshold boundary may cause flickering if the grid is updated frequently with noisy density estimates [S1, unofficial].
-- **Boundaries:** Voxels outside the AABB must be handled explicitly (e.g., marked as empty) [S1, unofficial].
-- **Degenerate Input:** If the NeRF model is not trained, densities may be uniform, leading to an all-occupied or all-empty grid [S1, unofficial].
